.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt FFMPEG 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ffmpeg
.Nd convert, play and record audio
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar global-options
.Op Ar input-options
.Fl i Ar input
.Op Ar output-options
.Ar output
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
converts audio files and reads or writes the OSS sound device.
It is installed in the GNU root with shared libraries and built-in audio
codecs, under LGPL 2.1 or later.
GPL and nonfree components and external codec libraries are disabled.
.Pp
The input formats are WAV, MP3, FLAC, Ogg, AAC, MOV and raw S16LE PCM.
Decoders include MP3, FLAC, Vorbis, Opus, AAC and PCM.
Output is WAV or raw PCM, or the OSS device.
The file and pipe protocols are enabled; network protocols are disabled.
The filters include
.Cm aresample ,
.Cm aformat
and
.Cm volume .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i Ar input
Read an input file or device.
Input options precede the corresponding
.Fl i .
.It Fl f Ar format
Select the format of the following input or output.
Use
.Cm oss
for the sound device.
.It Fl ar Ar rate
Set the sample rate in Hz.
.It Fl ac Ar channels
Set the channel count.
.It Fl c:a Ar codec
Select the audio encoder, such as
.Cm pcm_s16le .
.It Fl t Ar seconds
Limit the output duration.
.It Fl af Ar filters
Apply audio filters, such as
.Cm volume=0.5 .
.It Fl y
Replace an existing output file.
.It Fl devices , Fl decoders , Fl encoders , Fl formats , Fl filters
List the features of this build.
.It Fl L
Print the license.
.It Fl h
Print the command's help.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/dsp
.It Pa /dev/dsp
OSS playback and capture device.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Convert an MP3 to signed 16-bit WAV:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ffmpeg -i music.mp3 -c:a pcm_s16le music.wav
.Ed
.Pp
Play a file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ffmpeg -i music.flac -ar 48000 -ac 2 -f oss /dev/dsp
.Ed
.Pp
Record five seconds of stereo audio:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ffmpeg -f oss -ar 48000 -ac 2 -i /dev/dsp -t 5 take.wav
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ffprobe 1 ,
.Xr mixer 1 ,
.Xr dsp 4
.Sh LIMITS
This build has no video decoders or encoders.
The sound driver determines the rates, channels and formats available
through OSS.
